{"schema_version": 4, "name": "tumor-microenvironment", "title": "Tumor microenvironment (headline experiment) + full figure suite", "created": "2026-09-09", "status": "complete", "design_status": "complete", "implementation_status": "complete", "simulation_status": "ran", "phase": "Evaluate", "question": "Does the ported model reproduce tumor-tcell's headline experiment\n(tumor_microenvironment_experiment, id '5') \u2014 a central tumor mass ringed by\nT cells under the three CODEX conditions \u2014 and its full analysis figure suite?\n", "study_card": {"goal": "Reproduce the paper's headline simulation and the exact figures its analysis produces.", "mechanism": "Ring-seeded tumor mass + T cells (no-T / 25% PD1+ / 75% PD1+); IFNg-driven conversion + contact killing + exhaustion. Figures mirror individual_analysis: population-by-state, divisions, deaths-by-type, 8-panel snapshots, video.", "expected_result": "The full figure suite renders with the paper's cell-state colors (TAG_COLORS) over the YlOrBr IFNg field; the 25% PD1+ headline shows conversion, divisions, and (contact) killing.", "main_expert_question": "At the paper's full scale (1200 cells, 3 days) do the population/death curves match the published figures quantitatively?"}, "biological_summary": "This is the ported analogue of the paper's headline in-silico experiment (Hickey, Agmon et\nal., Cell Systems 2024, Figure 3): a tumor mass with T cells, run under the three conditions\nthe paper compares \u2014 no T cells, 25% PD1+ (mostly active, memory-like T cells from ex-vivo\n2HC treatment), and 75% PD1+ (mostly exhausted). In the paper this is 1,200 tumor cells + 12\nT cells over 3 days; here it is run at a tractable scale with the same mechanism. The paper's\nkey result: T cells that start more active (25% PD1+) drive the IFNg-mediated conversion of\nproliferative PDL1n tumor cells into the arrested PDL1p state earlier and more strongly than\n75% PD1+ T cells, holding the tumor to ~1,000 cells vs ~3,000 (75% PD1+) vs ~5,000 (no T) at\n60 h \u2014 despite a nearly identical number of kills in the two T-cell conditions. So control of\ngrowth comes from conversion, not raw killing.\n\nThe study emits the same figures the original's individual_analysis produces \u2014 tumor and\nT-cell population-by-state timeseries, cumulative divisions, cumulative deaths by type, an\n8-panel spatial snapshot montage, and a spatial animation/GIF (the video analogue) \u2014 using\nthe paper's cell-state colors (PDL1n=indianred, PDL1p=skyblue, PD1n=darkorange,\nPD1p=limegreen) over the YlOrBr IFNg field. A cross-condition panel compares tumor count\nacross no-T / 25% / 75% PD1+.\n", "expected_behavior": [{"name": "reproduces_headline_suite", "en": "The headline experiment runs and produces the original's full analysis figure suite with matching colors.", "measure": {"kind": "qualitative", "of": "population-by-state, divisions, deaths-by-type, snapshot montage, and animation all render"}, "expect": {"op": "renders", "of": "all figures produced; 25% PD1+ shows IFNg-driven conversion and divisions/killing"}}], "behavior_tests": [{"name": "reproduces_headline_suite", "measure": {"kind": "qualitative", "of": "the 6-figure suite + cross-condition comparison"}, "expect": {"op": "renders", "of": "all figures render with TAG_COLORS / YlOrBr"}, "result": "PASS: population(tumor/tcell), divisions, deaths, snapshots, animation, and cross-condition comparison all rendered"}], "report": {"title": "Tumor microenvironment \u2014 headline experiment", "verdict": "passing-with-caveats", "confidence": "medium", "evidence_quality": "qualitative", "objective": "Reproduce the paper's headline simulation and figure suite.", "conclusion": "The ported headline experiment runs under all three CODEX conditions and reproduces\ntumor-tcell's full analysis figure suite (population-by-state, divisions, deaths-by-type,\nspatial snapshot montage, animation) with the paper's cell-state colors over the YlOrBr\nIFNg field.\n", "caveat": "Tractable scale (60 tumors, 600 ticks, single seed) \u2014 a faithful reproduction of the\nfigure suite and mechanism, not the paper's full 1200-cell / 3-day quantitative curves.\nDeath events are sparse at this scale/time.\n"}, "readouts": ["tumor & T-cell population-by-state over time", "cumulative divisions; cumulative deaths by type", "8-panel spatial snapshots + animation over the IFNg field", "cross-condition tumor count (no-T / 25% / 75% PD1+)"], "canonical_runs": [{"name": "headline-3-conditions", "script": "studies/tumor-microenvironment/sims/run.py"}], "visualizations": [{"name": "population_tumor", "path": "viz/population_tumor.html"}, {"name": "population_tcell", "path": "viz/population_tcell.html"}, {"name": "divisions", "path": "viz/divisions.html"}, {"name": "deaths", "path": "viz/deaths.html"}, {"name": "snapshots", "path": "viz/snapshots.html"}, {"name": "spatial_animation", "path": "viz/spatial_animation.html"}, {"name": "spatial_large_scale", "path": "viz/spatial_large_scale.html"}, {"name": "tumor_count_by_condition", "path": "viz/tumor_count_by_condition.html"}], "baseline": [{"name": "baseline", "composite": "viva_tumor_tcell.composites.microenvironment.tumor_microenvironment", "params": {"n_tumors": 60, "n_tcells": 12, "pd1_positive_frac": 0.25}}], "interface": {"composite": null, "config": {}, "inputs": [], "outputs": [], "emitter": null}, "runs": [{"run_id": "ad5473fde0364683b7d7410a2199508f", "spec_id": "tumor-microenvironment", "label": "tumor-microenvironment: 25% PD1+ (representative)", "sim_name": "tumor-microenvironment: 25% PD1+ (representative)", "variant": null, "composite": null, "params": {}, "n_steps": null, "status": "ran", "started_at": "2026-09-09T12:15:16Z", "completed_at": null, "db_path": "studies/tumor-microenvironment/runs.db", "source": "simulations", "started_at_iso": "2026-09-09T12:15:16Z", "stale": false, "params_summary": ""}, {"run_id": "3799f330fd6942809288900f45124c9a", "spec_id": "viva_tumor_tcell